# Reverse-engineering artifacts kept locally only, never committed: Apple binary
# decompilations and interop probes. Removed from history; do not re-add.
/xpcdump/
/xpcDistributed/
/Tools/
# The XPC platform-matrix probes. Same category as the above, kept out of history by the
# same rule -- but unlike the decompilations these are *cited by committed code*: the plan's
# "Verified API facts" carries ~20 measured rows and tells you to re-run them, and source
# comments name individual rows. So the probes live here on disk and the citations say
# "local only". If you clone this repo fresh, those rows are prose you cannot reproduce;
# one has already changed answer under an OS update.
/docs/xpc-platform-matrix/
